                      gamut: third-party notices

gamut itself is under LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE, at your option, and the
work carried in its own source tree is accounted for in REUSE.toml with the
texts it names in LICENSES/. This file is the third part: the crates compiled
into the binary. Nothing here is gamut's own code, and nothing here is
optional at runtime — every crate below is statically linked, so its notice
travels with the program.

It is generated by `cargo about` from Cargo.lock, for the two targets the
package is built for, and bin/release rewrites it. Do not edit it by hand: the
stamp on the first line is the lock this was generated from, and CI fails if
it is not the lock in the tree. Adding a dependency means running bin/release,
or regenerating with

    cargo about generate --frozen packaging/about.hbs

